cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this experiment, its data or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Kubernetes autoscaling: HPA vs KEDA, CPU vs request rate"
abstract: >-
  A controlled experiment on Azure Kubernetes Service that separates the effect of the scaling metric
  (CPU vs request rate) from that of the autoscaler (the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler vs KEDA):
  180 open-loop load-test runs (2 services x 6 configurations x 3 load patterns x 5 repetitions) with
  per-request data, the code and manifests that produced them, the pre-registered analysis, and the
  research log of the undergraduate thesis "Analisis Pengaruh Jenis Metrik Penskalaan dan Mekanisme
  Autoscaler (HPA vs KEDA) terhadap Responsivitas dan Efisiensi Resource Aplikasi Microservices pada
  Kubernetes".
type: software
